{!<div class="election-map-host" data-election-map-source="president-2025-r1"></div>!}

Our candidate, **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]**, finishes on **[+
pres_2025_player_result +]%**; all Left candidates together reach **[+
pres_2025_field_result +]%**.

[? if pres_2025_united_left: We entered through **[+
pres_2025_nomination_method +]** and receive one verdict rather than an
arithmetic promise that two electorates would combine. [? if
pres_2025_unity_effect >= 0: Members recognise the nomination as legitimate,
so losing factions help carry the result.?][? if pres_2025_unity_effect < 0:
The nomination never convinced every current, and some activists sit out the
campaign they were told was united.?]?]

[? if pres_2025_candidate_level = -3: The result is a shattering defeat. Donors
close their books, organisers stop answering calls and every New Left faction
demands a leadership reckoning before the parliamentary campaign.?]
[? if pres_2025_candidate_level = -2: The candidate falls below a defensible
base. KO attracts tactical voters, local teams begin conserving resources and
the leadership can no longer dismiss its challengers as impatient.?]
[? if pres_2025_candidate_level = -1: The result is neither collapse nor
vindication. We keep a presidential electorate, but faction leaders reopen the
strategy while journalists ask which larger camp will squeeze us next.?]
[? if pres_2025_candidate_level = 1: The base holds. Members have proof that a
Left ballot remains useful, and the immediate tactical flight to KO slows.?]
[? if pres_2025_candidate_level = 2: A strong result gives our organisers an
electorate they can find again and forces coalition partners to bargain with
the Left as a national camp.?]
[? if pres_2025_candidate_level >= 3: The campaign breaks through the old
ceiling. Candidate authority, volunteers and media follow; every faction now
wants to define what the new electorate voted for.?]

[? if pres_2025_leadership_defeat: **[+ pres_2025_left_candidate +]** finishes
behind Zandberg. A strong combined Left field cannot erase the challenge to New
Left's leadership, donors or claim to direct a future common list.?]
[? if pres_2025_radical_result >= 20: [+ pres_2025_konf_surname +] and Braun together command a
large radical-right electorate. Their rivalry no longer makes either one a
side show.?]
[? if pres_2025_stanowski_breakout = 1: Stanowski's result is no commentary
candidacy: **[+ pres_2025_r1_display_stanowski +]%** gives Kanał Zero a
national electorate, humiliates the centrist campaign that assumed media
outsiders belonged to it and leaves a ready-made organisation waiting after
the count.?]

[? if pres_2025_first_round_winner: Elected in the first round: **[+
pres_2025_winner +] — [+ pres_2025_first_round_winner_share +]%**.?]
[? if not pres_2025_first_round_winner: Runoff: **[+ pres_2025_finalist_a +] vs
[+ pres_2025_finalist_b +]**?]

- @first_round_winner_record
- @runoff_broker

@first_round_winner_record
title: Record the first-round election
view-if: pres_2025_first_round_winner = 1

The campaign does not bargain for transfers: the electorate has already filled
the office. Every party now decides how to live with the winner it produced.

- @poland_event_queue: Let the result reach the events desk

@runoff_broker
title: Open the inter-round support market
new-page: true
view-if: pres_2025_first_round_winner = 0

= Two weeks, no automatic transfers

[? if not pres_2025_left_finalist: The Left is eliminated. Razem voters,
government-left voters and abstainers do not move as one bloc. The endorsement
can buy a programme, maximise anti-right turnout, or preserve autonomy.?]
[? if pres_2025_left_finalist: A Left candidate has reached the runoff. The
campaign must now persuade KO, centrist and anti-system electorates without
ceasing to be a Left candidacy.?]

The fortnight has two halves. First the party settles its own line, which every
newsroom will report within the hour. Then it spends what that line is worth on
the electorates the first round left without a candidate.

- @runoff_accord
- @runoff_immediate
- @runoff_free
- @runoff_razem_accord
- @runoff_razem_endorse
- @runoff_razem_free
- @runoff_insurgent
- @runoff_broad

@runoff_accord
title: Negotiate a written accord with [+ pres_2025_finalist_a +]
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources. Endorse finalist A only after named social, judicial and constitutional commitments.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 0 and pres_2025_razem_finalist = 0
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot finance a joint runoff operation.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 2;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target = Q.pres_2025_finalist_a_key;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Negotiated accord with " + Q.pres_2025_finalist_a;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = 1.1;
if (Q.pres_2025_finalist_a_key == "ko") Q.ko_relation += 6;
else if (Q.pres_2025_finalist_a_key == "right") Q.pis_relation += 4;
else if (Q.pres_2025_finalist_a_key == "holownia") Q.p2050_relation += 6;
else if (["mentzen", "braun"].includes(Q.pres_2025_finalist_a_key)) {
    Q.konf_relation += 3;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 6;
}
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left prices an endorsement of " + Q.pres_2025_finalist_a;
!}

The talks take four days and produce two pages. Named commitments, named
deadlines, a published text: what the pen will sign on labour law, what it will
refer to the courts, which appointments will be consulted before they are made.
**[+ pres_2025_finalist_a +]** signs because a fortnight is short and our
voters are not otherwise coming.

Nothing in the document is enforceable. Its value is that it exists in public,
so that a broken clause becomes a story rather than a private disappointment,
and so that our own organisers can campaign for something instead of merely
against somebody.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_immediate
title: Endorse [+ pres_2025_finalist_b +] immediately
subtitle: Ask Left voters to move at once without securing a written programme.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 0 and pres_2025_razem_finalist = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target = Q.pres_2025_finalist_b_key;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Immediate endorsement of " + Q.pres_2025_finalist_b;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0.45;
if (Q.pres_2025_finalist_b_key == "ko") Q.ko_relation += 4;
else if (Q.pres_2025_finalist_b_key == "right") Q.pis_relation += 3;
else if (Q.pres_2025_finalist_b_key == "holownia") Q.p2050_relation += 4;
else if (["mentzen", "braun"].includes(Q.pres_2025_finalist_b_key)) {
    Q.konf_relation += 2;
    Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
}
Q.public_trust += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 5;
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_left_ownership += -4;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left immediately endorses " + Q.pres_2025_finalist_b;
!}

The statement goes out on the Monday morning, before anybody has been asked for
anything. It is the clean version of the argument: this is a choice between two
presidencies, one of them would be a catastrophe for people we represent, and
we are not going to spend the fortnight pretending otherwise.

It also spends the only leverage the first round produced. **[+
pres_2025_finalist_b +]**'s staff are polite and busy, and by Wednesday the
question of what our voters were promised has stopped being asked in the
building.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_free
title: Release voters without an endorsement
subtitle: Preserve the party's autonomy and surrender organised influence over the result.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 0 and pres_2025_razem_finalist = 0
on-arrival: pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Free vote"; pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "none"; pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0; progressives_dissent += 3; razem_dissent -= 2; party_unity -= 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += -5; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += -5; news_headline = "The Left refuses to command its voters between the two named finalists"

The wording is careful and everyone understands it anyway: our voters are
adults, the ballot contains no candidate of ours, and the party will not spend
its authority telling a million people whom to prefer between two men who
offered them nothing.

Half the party thinks this is the only honest position available. The other
half spends the fortnight being asked on television whether the Left is
indifferent to the difference, and discovers that there is no short answer.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_razem_accord
title: Negotiate a social accord with the Razem finalist
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Back a rival Left campaign in exchange for written labour, housing and public-service commitments.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 0 and pres_2025_razem_finalist = 1
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The party cannot finance a joint runoff operation.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Negotiated Left accord"; pres_2025_transfer_strength = 1.1; pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "razem"; razem_relation += 7; party_unity += 1; labor_credibility += 2; news_headline = "New Left and Razem negotiate a social programme for the runoff"

The negotiation is harder than it should be, because both delegations know that
whatever is signed will be read as a verdict on the last two years. What comes
out is a labour, housing and public-service text that neither camp could have
written alone, and a joint appearance nobody in either headquarters expected to
see this year.

Our people work for it. Some of them work for it in the specific manner of
those who have just been overtaken and intend to be visible about their
loyalty.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_razem_endorse
title: Endorse the Razem finalist immediately
subtitle: Accept Razem's lead without negotiating a joint programme or guarantee.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 0 and pres_2025_razem_finalist = 1
on-arrival: pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Immediate Razem endorsement"; pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0.55; pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "razem"; razem_relation += 4; public_trust += 1; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "New Left asks its voters to back the Razem finalist"

No conditions, no text, no ceremony: the Left has a candidate in the second
round and it is not ours, and the party says so within the hour. Outside the
two headquarters this reads as maturity, which is worth something in a fortnight
where every other camp is haggling in public.

Inside, it is understood as the leadership declining to test whether it could
have extracted anything. That question will be asked again at the next council
meeting, with the result already known.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_razem_free
title: Release voters without endorsing Razem
subtitle: No organised transfer; preserves autonomy but deepens the leadership contest on the Left.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 0 and pres_2025_razem_finalist = 1
on-arrival: pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Free vote with a Razem finalist"; pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0; pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "none"; razem_relation -= 7; party_unity -= 2; news_headline = "New Left refuses to endorse the Razem finalist without campaigning against it"

The formula is that the party will not campaign against a Left candidate and
will not campaign for one either. It is defensible for about a day, until a
journalist asks whether there is any circumstance in which New Left would work
for a president from Razem, and the answer takes too long.

Razem's organisers draw the obvious conclusion and stop asking. Whatever
happens on the first of June, the two organisations will enter it further apart
than they left the first round.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_insurgent
title: Run a worker-and-housing insurgency against both old blocs
subtitle: Keep a distinct Left programme and refuse the easier shelter of a broad KO front.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 1
on-arrival: pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Left insurgency"; pres_2025_runoff_campaign = "Left insurgency"; pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0.6; pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.55; labor_credibility += 5; ko_relation -= 5; psl_relation -= 2; turnout_readiness += 4; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 9; public_mood_pending_social_spending_salience += 8; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -4; news_headline = "The Left enters the runoff without dissolving into the democratic camp"

The fortnight is run as a continuation rather than a conversion. Wages, rents,
waiting lists; the same argument at a higher volume, in the towns where the
first round produced numbers nobody in Warsaw expected.

KO's offer of an umbrella is declined in public, which costs us their machine
and buys something they cannot supply: a candidacy that means the same thing on
the first of June as it meant on the eighteenth of May. Turnout among people
who do not usually vote is now the whole strategy.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@runoff_broad
title: Offer KO and the centre a constitutional unity presidency
subtitle: Cost: 2 resources.
view-if: pres_2025_player_finalist = 1
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The joint turnout operation cannot be financed.
on-arrival: resources -= 2; pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Broad constitutional front"; pres_2025_runoff_campaign = "Broad constitutional front"; pres_2025_transfer_strength = 1.2; pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.75; ko_relation += 7; p2050_relation += 5; psl_relation += 3; razem_dissent += 2; turnout_readiness += 5; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 8; public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += -4; news_headline = "A Left finalist offers a constitutional majority without abandoning the programme"

The offer is precise about what it is not: no coalition, no programme merger,
no promise about a future government. What it does promise is a presidency that
every democratic party can live under — courts, appointments, the veto used by
one published standard — and it invites KO, Poland 2050 and PSL to campaign for
that rather than for us.

They accept, with the enthusiasm of people who have run out of alternatives.
Mayors open their offices; the centrist press discovers reasons to be calm.
Razem's members watch a Left candidacy acquire liberal chaperones and say so.

- @pres25_support_market: Open the inter-round support market

@pres25_support_market
title: Inter-round support market
new-page: true

= Two negotiations — [+ pres_2025_support_actions_remaining +] remain

[? if pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "none": The party is asking nobody for
anything, which does not mean the fortnight is empty. Organisers, turnout and
the electorates nobody else is courting are all still available.?][? if
pres_2025_runoff_support_target != "none": Our line is settled. What remains is
the harder work: the eliminated electorates belong to nobody, and each of them
has to be approached in its own language.?]

Each operation can be used once. None of them delivers a bloc; they change how
much of one electorate is reachable in fourteen days.

- @pres25_support_holownia
- @pres25_support_committees
- @pres25_support_stanowski
- @pres25_support_movements
- @pres25_support_left
- @pres25_support_radical
- @pres25_support_turnout
- @pres25_support_release

@pres25_support_holownia
title: Offer Poland 2050 an oversight and public-service accord
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. The most persuadable eliminated electorate, and the most expensive.
view-if: pres_2025_support_holownia = 0 and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "holownia" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "holownia"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No joint operation with Poland 2050 can be staffed.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_holownia = 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_holownia =
    0.06 + ((Number(Q.p2050_relation) || 0) >= 35 ? 0.04 : 0);
Q.p2050_relation += 4;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.12;
Q.news_headline =
    "Poland 2050 and the Left agree an oversight package for the second round";
!}

**[+ pres_2025_centre_surname +]** and the Poland 2050 organisers do not
deliver voters and say so at the start of the meeting.
What they can deliver is a text: parliamentary oversight of appointments, a
public-service audit, a commitment that neither camp treats institutional
reform as a bargaining chip after the ballot.

It is published jointly, which is the point. Their voters are the least
tribal electorate in the country and the most responsive to being given a
reason rather than an instruction.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_committees
title: Go after the eliminated committees' secular Left voters
subtitle: Free. Senyszyn's and the independents' voters are close to us and nobody else is asking.
view-if: pres_2025_support_committees = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_support_committees = 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_other = 0.09;
Q.organiser_energy -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.10;
Q.public_mood_pending_secular_state_support += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left courts the electorates the smaller committees leave behind";
!}

Senyszyn's voters are older, secular, and were voting against Lewica's
organisation rather than against its programme. Bartoszewicz's are neither left
nor right but comprehensively finished with parties. Between them they are
worth more than the row they occupy in the model.

The operation is unglamorous — regional radio, three interviews, a letter to
committees that no other campaign bothered to write. It works because nobody
else considered these people worth the postage.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_stanowski
title: Take the interview on Kanał Zero
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Enormous reach on somebody else's terms.
view-if: pres_2025_support_stanowski = 0 and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "stanowski" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "stanowski"
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The campaign cannot clear the schedule or the production costs.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_stanowski = 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_stanowski = Q.pres_2025_stanowski_breakout
    ? 0.16
    : 0.10;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.young_support += 1;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += Q.pres_2025_stanowski_breakout
    ? 0.16
    : 0.08;
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left takes the long interview in front of an audience no party owns";
!}

Two hours, no format, no agreed questions, an audience of young men who have
never watched a party broadcast in their lives. Stanowski asks about money
first and rights later and does not pretend to be neutral about either.

There is no way to control what is clipped from it. There is also no other room
in Poland where this many people who dislike all of us will sit still for two
hours, and the campaign's own footage is worthless by comparison.

[? if pres_2025_stanowski_breakout = 1: This time the audience is also an
electorate. Stanowski can point to **[+ pres_2025_r1_display_stanowski +]%**,
and the interview is bargaining with a campaign-sized constituency rather than
borrowing reach from a broadcaster.?]

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_movements
title: Put unions, tenants and equality organisations on a turnout committee
subtitle: Free. Costs organisers rather than money; refused for a radical-right target.
view-if: pres_2025_support_movements = 0
choose-if: pres_2025_runoff_support_target != "right" and pres_2025_runoff_support_target != "mentzen" and pres_2025_runoff_support_target != "braun"
unavailable-subtitle: The movements will not staff an operation for this candidate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_support_movements = 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_left =
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_left) || 0) + 0.07;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_razem =
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_razem) || 0) + 0.07;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.55;
Q.organiser_energy -= 4;
Q.turnout_readiness += 3;
Q.feminist_trust += 2;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += 7;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += 6;
Q.news_headline =
    "Unions, tenants' groups and equality organisations build a runoff turnout machine";
!}

It is not an endorsement and it is not run from party headquarters. Three
federations, a tenants' network and the abortion-rights organisations put their
own names on a committee whose only function is getting people to a polling
station on the first of June.

They can do things a party cannot: knock on the doors of people who hate
parties, and be believed when they say the difference matters. It empties our
offices for a fortnight to make it possible.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_left
title: Bind the other Left campaign's voters into the same fortnight
subtitle: Free. Available while two Left candidacies have to explain themselves to one electorate.
view-if: pres_2025_support_left = 0 and pres_2025_united_left = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_support_left = 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_left =
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_left) || 0) + 0.10;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_razem =
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_razem) || 0) + 0.10;
Q.razem_cooperation += 4;
Q.party_unity += 2;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.15;
Q.news_headline =
    "Both Left campaigns tell the same electorate the same thing about the runoff";
!}

The two headquarters that spent five months distinguishing themselves now have
to explain to the same people why the distinction does not apply for fourteen
days. It is done with a joint appearance rather than a document, because a
document would take longer than the fortnight allows.

Nobody pretends the argument is over. What the operation buys is that neither
electorate hears its own campaign shrug about the second round, which is how a
Left vote turns into an abstention.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_radical
title: Contest [+ pres_2025_konf_surname +]'s voters on wages, rents and the cost of the state
subtitle: No endorsement is sought or offered. A raid on an electorate that despises us.
view-if: pres_2025_support_radical = 0 and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "mentzen" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "mentzen"
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_support_radical = 1;
Q.pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_mentzen = 0.05;
Q.pres_2025_trade_boost_braun = 0.02;
Q.labor_credibility += 1;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 3;
Q.minority_safety -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent += 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 8;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += -4;
Q.news_headline =
    "The runoff campaign contests the radical right's electorate instead of conceding it";
!}

The argument is made without a single concession on rights, which is what makes
it difficult: a young man renting a room in Rzeszów is being robbed, and the
people telling him it is the fault of foreigners have a tax programme that will
leave his mother's ward without the state they claim to defend.

Some of them listen. The cost is paid at home, where a fortnight of campaigning
in that vocabulary is read by our own activists as the beginning of the
concession the leadership swore it would never make.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_turnout
title: Spend the slot on registration, transport and ballot protection
subtitle: Free fallback. Creates voters instead of claiming somebody else's.
view-if: pres_2025_support_turnout = 0
on-arrival: pres_2025_support_turnout = 1; pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1; pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.42; turnout_readiness += 3; local_network += 2; news_headline = "One bargaining slot becomes buses, certificates and precinct observers"

Certificates for people voting away from home, minibuses in counties where the
polling station is nine kilometres from the estate, and an observer in every
precinct where the first round produced a protocol somebody had to correct.

There is no negotiation and nobody to thank. It is the least interesting thing
on the board and, in a race decided by a point, the least likely to be wasted.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_release
title: Close a negotiation without a deal
subtitle: Guaranteed fallback. No transfer, no obligations, no ownership of the outcome.
view-if: pres_2025_support_release = 0
on-arrival: pres_2025_support_release = 1; pres_2025_support_actions_remaining -= 1; party_unity += 1; movement_autonomy += 2; news_headline = "The Left leaves one runoff negotiation deliberately empty"

The meeting happens and produces nothing, which is a decision rather than a
failure. Every organisation in the room keeps its own line, and the party keeps
the ability to say afterwards that it promised no one anything.

In a fortnight where every camp is acquiring debts, refusing one is worth
something. It is worth nothing at all on the count.

- @pres25_support_next
- @pres25_support_done

@pres25_support_next
title: Return to the support market
view-if: pres_2025_support_actions_remaining > 0
go-to: pres25_support_market

@pres25_support_done
title: Close the negotiations and wait for the second ballot
view-if: pres_2025_support_actions_remaining <= 0
go-to: pres25_torun_democratic if (pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "ko" or pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "holownia") and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "mentzen" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "mentzen"; pres25_torun_pis if pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "right" and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "mentzen" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "mentzen"; poland_event_queue

@pres25_torun_democratic
title: A beer becomes the democratic camp's runoff photograph
subtitle: Mentzen offers an audience, a pub and eight terms the Left did not negotiate
new-page: true
view-if: (pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "ko" or pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "holownia") and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "mentzen" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "mentzen"
on-arrival: {!
Q.mentzen_declaration_2025_done = 1;
Q.mentzen_kingmaker_active = 1;
Q.pres_2025_torun_route = "democratic";
Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key = Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target;
Q.pres_2025_torun_target_name = Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "ko"
    ? Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate
    : Q.pres_2025_centre_candidate;
Q.konf_normalisation += 8;
Q.news_headline = Q.pres_2025_torun_target_name +
    " drinks a beer with Mentzen in the fortnight between ballots";
!}

= The fortnight between ballots — Piwo z Mentzenem

[? if pres_2025_konf_candidate = "Sławomir Mentzen": <span
class="party-konf"><b>Sławomir Mentzen</b></span>, eliminated on **[+
pres_2025_r1_display_mentzen +]%**, invites both finalists to his Toruń pub and
YouTube programme.?]

[? if pres_2025_konf_candidate = "Krzysztof Bosak": <span
class="party-konf"><b>Krzysztof Bosak</b></span> leaves Konfederacja with **[+
pres_2025_r1_display_mentzen +]%** and no finalist. Party chair **Sławomir
Mentzen** then invites both finalists to his Toruń pub and YouTube programme,
turning Bosak's electorate into his own inter-round audience.?]

**[+ pres_2025_torun_target_name +]** goes, drinks the beer
and lets the cameras hold the glass beside Mentzen. Nationalists resent the
visitor; the democratic camp's left flank sees its endorsement turned into
somebody else's normalisation campaign.

[? if pres_2025_torun_target_name != "Radosław Sikorski": Sikorski joins the
table, and the three-man beer clip travels further than the refusal to sign the
whole declaration.?]

[? if pres_2025_torun_target_name = "Radosław Sikorski": The foreign minister
needs no second KO figure in the photograph; the two-man beer clip carries his
Atlanticist campaign into Mentzen's nationalist audience.?]

[? if pres_2025_torun_target_key = "ko": Tusk approves the reach and accepts
that the picture will anger voters who expected the democratic candidate to
keep Mentzen at arm's length.?]

[? if pres_2025_torun_target_key = "holownia": Poland 2050 approves the reach
as proof that the centre can speak outside the old blocs; KO resents lending
Sikorski and a democratic-camp photograph to a rival finalist.?]

Mentzen puts an eight-point Toruń Declaration on the table: no tax rises, no
Ukrainian accession to NATO, no further surrender of sovereignty and no new
gun controls among the tests. The finalist refuses to sign all eight and agrees
only where the campaign can defend the point. That distinction survives in the
full recording; the beer photograph travels without it.

Lewica now has three organisational positions. Each changes how much of our
endorsement still reaches a door in the last week.

- @pres25_torun_razem_withdraw
- @pres25_torun_progressive_instruction
- @pres25_torun_democratic_operation

@pres25_torun_razem_withdraw
title: Accept Razem's demand and withdraw the endorsement entirely
subtitle: Recover the independent Left line and remove our field operation from the finalist.
view-if: razem_split = 0 and (razem_in_left = 1 or (left_merger_structure = "federation" and merger_razem_present = 1 and razem_org_status != "departed"))
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "none";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Endorsement withdrawn after Piwo z Mentzenem";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus -= 0.55;
Q.razem_cooperation += 8;
Q.razem_dissent -= 6;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 9;
if (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "holownia") Q.p2050_relation -= 6;
Q.party_unity += 1;
Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
    "the withdrawal: no use of Lewica's name to validate the Toruń appearance";
Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
    "the finalist's campaign republishes our earlier endorsement beside the beer photograph";
Q.news_headline =
    "Razem keeps the Left inside one party by ending the runoff endorsement";
!}

The endorsement and canvass sheets are withdrawn in the same statement. Razem
stays inside a party willing to enforce a boundary; organisers already working
the finalist's lists are told that the work no longer carries Lewica's name.

KO calls the reversal a gift to PiS, and the target campaign loses the only
part of our first-round electorate that could be reached by an organised
instruction. The Left has recovered its line by making the runoff harder to
win.

- @pres25_torun_mirror: Put the written boundary to its final test

@pres25_torun_progressive_instruction
title: Reduce support to a bare instruction to vote
subtitle: No shared platforms and no canvassing; the endorsement survives without an operation.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Bare voting instruction after Piwo z Mentzenem";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = Math.min(
    0.35,
    Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0
);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus -= 0.25;
Q.razem_cooperation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent += 1;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.ko_relation -= 3;
if (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "holownia") Q.p2050_relation -= 2;
Q.organiser_energy += 2;
Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
    "the written limit of one voting instruction, with no shared platform or canvass";
Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
    "the finalist turns the beer clip into a shared platform and asks our MPs to carry it";
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica keeps a voting instruction and removes its field operation";
!}

The party says whom it prefers and nothing more. MPs may give the one-sentence
instruction; offices may not canvass, share a stage or distribute the Toruń
clip. Progressive currents can defend the boundary, but a line without a field
operation reaches fewer people than the endorsement negotiated after round one.

The democratic partners keep the name of our preferred candidate and lose the
organisers they expected to accompany it. They say publicly that abstention is
now being manufactured by people who know exactly what the alternative means.

- @pres25_torun_mirror: Put the written boundary to its final test

@pres25_torun_democratic_operation
title: Keep the endorsement and field operation unchanged
subtitle: Democratic partners retain every organiser; Razem and the progressives own the public objection.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Full democratic field operation after Piwo z Mentzenem";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength += 0.35;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.45;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 6;
Q.razem_dissent += 7;
Q.progressives_dissent += 6;
Q.ko_relation += 5;
if (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "holownia") Q.p2050_relation += 4;
Q.organiser_energy -= 3;
Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
    "the written refusal of the Toruń Declaration and any further policy concession";
Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
    "the finalist gives Mentzen a no-tax-rise line our agreement reserved for Parliament";
Q.news_headline =
    "The democratic runoff operation continues through the Toruń backlash";
!}

The endorsement, joint appearances and canvass lists remain where they were.
Democratic partners receive the operation they budgeted for and say, in public,
that nobody facing a PiS-backed presidency has the luxury of abandoning it over
a photograph.

Razem and the progressive currents answer in their own names. The field gain is
real; so is the lesson that a larger ally may borrow nationalist theatre and
still expect the Left to supply the doors.

- @pres25_torun_mirror: Put the written boundary to its final test

@pres25_torun_pis
title: The PiS-backed finalist submits a price list to Mentzen—and receives ours
subtitle: Campaigning for the right can buy terms, a Palace staff and a fight over its next nomination
new-page: true
view-if: pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "right" and pres_2025_finalist_a_key != "mentzen" and pres_2025_finalist_b_key != "mentzen"
on-arrival: {!
Q.mentzen_declaration_2025_done = 1;
Q.mentzen_kingmaker_active = 1;
Q.pres_2025_torun_route = "pis";
Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key = "right";
Q.pres_2025_torun_target_name = Q.pres_2025_right_candidate;
Q.konf_normalisation += 10;
Q.news_headline = Q.pres_2025_right_candidate +
    " faces Mentzen's eight points while Lewica prices its runoff work";
!}

= The fortnight between ballots — Two price lists

**[+ pres_2025_konf_candidate +]** brings **[+
pres_2025_r1_display_mentzen +]%** of first-round voters; Mentzen brings the Toruń Declaration
to his pub: no tax rises, no Ukrainian accession to NATO, sovereignty clauses
and no new gun controls among eight points. **[+ pres_2025_right_candidate +]**
signals readiness to sign. Mentzen withholds a formal endorsement and says
there is no reason to vote for the democratic opponent.

Lewica is already bargaining with the PiS-backed finalist. If our endorsement
is to become campaigning, PiS must receive its own price list. One item is
personnel: move the right toward Morawiecki's state-and-transfer politics and
away from the harder culture-war names without pretending the ballot can still
be changed.

- @pres25_pis_morawiecki_staff
- @pres25_pis_social_price
- @pres25_pis_instruction_only

@pres25_pis_morawiecki_staff
title: Make Morawiecki's administrators the price of Palace campaigning
subtitle: Secure a personnel lever and carry a PiS-backed candidate through the last week.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength += 0.30;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.35;
Q.pis_relation += 5;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 5;
Q.razem_dissent += 6;
Q.progressives_dissent += 7;
Q.pis_solidarist_share += 3;
Q.pis_sovereigntist_strength -= 2;
Q.far_right_agenda -= 2;
if (Q.pres_2025_right_candidate == "Mateusz Morawiecki") {
    Q.pres_2025_morawiecki_push =
        "Morawiecki's own state-and-transfer team staffs the Palace";
    Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
        "the written condition that Morawiecki staff the Palace from his state-and-transfer wing and not bind it to all eight Toruń points";
    Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
        "the candidate signs all eight points and announces hard-line culture-war appointments instead";
} else {
    Q.pres_2025_morawiecki_push =
        "Morawiecki-aligned Palace staff and first claim on the right's next nomination";
    Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
        "the written condition of Morawiecki-aligned Palace staff, a future nomination lever and no signature binding the Palace to all eight points";
    Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
        "the candidate signs all eight points, announces a hard-line Palace slate and disowns the succession bargain";
}
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica prices Palace campaigning in staff and the right's next succession";
!}

[? if pres_2025_right_candidate = "Mateusz Morawiecki": Morawiecki is already
on the ballot. The bargain therefore governs who staffs his Palace and whether
his own state-and-transfer wing, rather than PiS's harder factions, owns the
presidency. Nothing is swapped retroactively.?]

[? if pres_2025_right_candidate != "Mateusz Morawiecki": **[+
pres_2025_right_candidate +]** remains on the ballot. The written price places
Morawiecki-aligned administrators in the Palace and gives that wing the first
claim on the next nomination; it does not replace today's candidate after the
first round.?]

Our organisers campaign on the personnel clause and the transfers it is meant
to protect. PiS gains a field operation it could not command, while Razem and
the progressive currents acquire evidence that the party has moved from a
tactical vote to staffing a right-wing presidency.

- @pres25_torun_mirror: Put the written personnel clause to its final test

@pres25_pis_social_price
title: Publish a social price list and leave PiS's personnel fight alone
subtitle: Protect transfers, labour inspection and services without endorsing the succession bargain.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength += 0.15;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus += 0.22;
Q.pis_relation += 3;
Q.labor_credibility += 2;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 4;
Q.progressives_dissent += 5;
Q.pres_2025_morawiecki_push =
    "No personnel lever; a social price list only";
Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
    "the written no-cuts guarantee for transfers, labour inspection and public services";
Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
    "the finalist signs every Toruń point, including the tax lock that makes our guarantees impossible";
Q.news_headline =
    "The Left publishes the social cost of campaigning for the PiS-backed finalist";
!}

The list is short enough to read on television: no cut to family transfers, a
funded labour inspectorate, hospital finance protected from the tax pledge and
no Palace veto of the agreed worker bills. PiS signs because it needs people
who can speak to voters outside its own organisation.

We keep out of the succession fight and lose the only opportunity to weaken
the culture-war wing through personnel. Progressive organisers still have to
explain why a written social floor justifies canvassing for a candidate who
signed Mentzen's whole declaration.

- @pres25_torun_mirror: Put the written social floor to its final test

@pres25_pis_instruction_only
title: Keep the endorsement but refuse a shared PiS campaign
subtitle: Preserve the tactical line, abandon the price list and accept a weaker transfer.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Tactical instruction without a shared PiS campaign";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = Math.min(
    0.25,
    Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0
);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus -= 0.30;
Q.pis_relation -= 5;
Q.razem_cooperation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 2;
Q.pres_2025_morawiecki_push =
    "Morawiecki lever proposed and refused";
Q.pres_2025_torun_red_line =
    "the written limit of no second meeting, shared platform or joint canvass";
Q.pres_2025_torun_breach =
    "the finalist takes a second meeting, signs all eight points and asks PiS offices to advertise our support";
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica keeps a tactical instruction and refuses to join the PiS field campaign";
!}

The party repeats the voting instruction and supplies no stage, canvasser or
price list. Our factions avoid becoming part of the PiS operation; the workers
and services we might have protected receive no paper guarantee at all.

PiS calls the position cowardice dressed as support. The candidate keeps our
name in the endorsement column and loses most of the reachable voters that an
actual joint operation might have moved.

- @pres25_torun_mirror: Put the written campaign limit to its final test

@pres25_torun_mirror
title: [+ pres_2025_torun_target_name +] breaks the line we put in writing
subtitle: The last week tests whether an endorsement is leverage or merely permission
new-page: true
view-if: pres_2025_torun_route = "democratic" or pres_2025_torun_route = "pis"
on-arrival: {!
Q.news_headline = Q.pres_2025_torun_target_name +
    " breaches the runoff terms agreed with Lewica";
!}

= The last week — The mirror

The written line was **[+ pres_2025_torun_red_line +]**. The breach is equally
plain: **[+ pres_2025_torun_breach +]**. Headquarters receives the clip before
the morning meeting and the explanation before noon: the finalist needed
[+ pres_2025_konf_surname +]'s voters, the campaign moved too quickly, and reopening the endorsement
now would only help the other person on the ballot.

[? if pres_2025_torun_route = "democratic": The democratic camp that asked us
to accept the beer as necessary now asks us to treat its own written limit as
optional. The Left can preserve the anti-right transfer only by teaching every
partner what our conditions cost to break.?]

[? if pres_2025_torun_route = "pis": The PiS-backed camp that accepted a
price for our canvass now treats that price as campaign stationery. A tactical
bargain with the right has reached the exact test our factions said it would.?]

- @pres25_breach_eat
- @pres25_breach_public
- @pres25_breach_pull

@pres25_breach_eat
title: Eat the breach and keep every organiser in the field
subtitle: Protect the transfer; make Lewica's written conditions cheaper next time.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_runoff_breach_shift = 0;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength += 0.10;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 4;
Q.razem_dissent += 6;
Q.progressives_dissent += 6;
Q.party_unity -= 3;
Q.public_trust -= 2;
if (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "right") Q.pis_relation += 2;
else Q.ko_relation += 2;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica absorbs the runoff breach and keeps its organisers in the field";
!}

No corrective statement is issued. The field operation keeps its lists and the
candidate keeps the full value of our endorsement. Faction representatives
record in the minutes that a written condition has been broken and discover
that minutes do not travel.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the swallowed breach into the count

@pres25_breach_public
title: Publish the breach and keep a reduced endorsement
subtitle: Recover a public boundary while taking some votes and trust out of the joint operation.
on-arrival: {!
Q.pres_2025_runoff_breach_shift = -0.25;
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength -= 0.20;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus -= 0.15;
Q.razem_cooperation += 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 2;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 1;
Q.party_unity -= 2;
Q.public_trust += 2;
Q.media_capacity += 1;
if (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "right") Q.pis_relation -= 6;
else Q.ko_relation -= 6;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica publishes the broken runoff clause and leaves a narrower endorsement in place";
!}

The agreement, timestamp and offending clip are released together. The party
still instructs voters to prefer the finalist, but no spokesperson describes
the campaign as a partner and several joint appearances disappear from the
calendar.

The public can see that the line existed. The finalist can see exactly how much
field strength survived our anger, and will remember that number in the next
negotiation.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the published breach into the count

@pres25_breach_pull
title: Pull the endorsement in the last week
subtitle: Enforce the agreement at the ballot box; measurably reduce the backed finalist's runoff coalition.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target == Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key) {
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target = "none";
}
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy =
    "Endorsement pulled after a written runoff breach";
Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus -= 0.60;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_breach_shift = -0.85;
Q.turnout_readiness -= 2;
Q.razem_cooperation += 4;
Q.razem_dissent -= 4;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 3;
Q.organiser_energy -= 2;
if (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == "right") Q.pis_relation -= 10;
else Q.ko_relation -= 10;
Q.news_headline =
    "Lewica pulls its runoff endorsement after the finalist breaks the written terms";
!}

Offices receive the stop order with days left. Printed material is pulped,
joint canvasses are cancelled and voters who heard one instruction on Monday
hear that the agreement behind it no longer exists on Friday.

The boundary is enforceable because the candidate loses something for crossing
it. The same fact makes the decision dangerous: the count will include people
our organisers might have reached and now deliberately will not.

- @poland_event_queue: Carry the withdrawn endorsement into the count

@calculate_presidential_runoff_2025
on-arrival: {!
const runoffMode25 =
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_calc_mode == "poll" ? "poll" : "result";
if (!Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy) {
    Q.pres_2025_transfer_strategy = "Not chosen";
}
if (!Q.pres_2025_runoff_final_push) {
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_final_push = "Not chosen";
}
if (!Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_name) {
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_name = "No candidate";
}
const finalistA = Q.pres_2025_finalist_a_key;
const finalistB = Q.pres_2025_finalist_b_key;
const supportTarget = Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_target;
const finalistNames = {};
finalistNames.ko = Q.pres_2025_ko_candidate || "Rafał Trzaskowski";
finalistNames.right = Q.pres_2025_right_candidate || "Karol Nawrocki";
finalistNames.left = Q.pres_2025_left_candidate;
finalistNames.razem = Q.pres_2025_razem_candidate || "Adrian Zandberg";
finalistNames.mentzen = Q.pres_2025_konf_candidate;
finalistNames.braun = "Grzegorz Braun";
finalistNames.holownia =
    Q.pres_2025_centre_candidate || "Szymon Hołownia";
finalistNames.stanowski = "Krzysztof Stanowski";
const historicalKoRight =
    finalistNames.ko == "Rafał Trzaskowski" &&
    (
        (finalistA == "ko" && finalistB == "right") ||
        (finalistA == "right" && finalistB == "ko")
    );
const resultAKey = historicalKoRight ? "ko" : finalistA;
const resultBKey = historicalKoRight ? "right" : finalistB;
let resultAShare;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_historical_pair = historicalKoRight ? 1 : 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_model = historicalKoRight
    ? "Historical Trzaskowski–Nawrocki calibration"
    : "Round-one shares and pair-specific voter alignment";
Q.pres_2025_runoff_r1_a =
    Number(Q["pres_2025_r1_" + resultAKey]) || 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_r1_b =
    Number(Q["pres_2025_r1_" + resultBKey]) || 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_transfer_a = 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_transfer_b = 0;
// The inter-round poll and the ballot are two readings of the same campaign
// under different noise, so the shock is drawn once at the start of the year.
const runoffShock25 = runoffMode25 == "poll"
    ? (Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_shock) || 0)
    : (Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_result_shock) || 0);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_variance = Math.round(
    runoffShock25 * (historicalKoRight ? 1.15 : 1.25) * 100
) / 100;
// Brokered support does not move a bloc: it moves the reachable fraction of
// one eliminated electorate, and only toward the candidate we actually named.
const tradeBoost25 = function(source) {
    return Math.max(0, Number(Q["pres_2025_trade_boost_" + source]) || 0);
};
const targetBonus25 =
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_target_bonus) || 0) +
    (Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_push_bonus) || 0);
const breachShift25 =
    Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == resultAKey
        ? (Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_breach_shift) || 0)
        : (Q.pres_2025_torun_target_key == resultBKey
            ? -(Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_breach_shift) || 0)
            : 0);
const allSourceKeys25 = [
    "ko", "right", "left", "razem", "mentzen",
    "braun", "holownia", "stanowski", "other"
];
if (historicalKoRight) {
    let brokered25 = 0;
    for (const source of allSourceKeys25) {
        if (source == "ko" || source == "right") continue;
        brokered25 +=
            Math.max(0, Number(Q["pres_2025_r1_" + source]) || 0) *
            tradeBoost25(source);
    }
    const marketShift25 = supportTarget == "ko"
        ? brokered25 + targetBonus25
        : (supportTarget == "right"
            ? -(brokered25 + targetBonus25)
            : 0);
    const endorsementShift = supportTarget == "ko"
        ? (Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0)
        : (supportTarget == "right"
            ? -(Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0)
            : 0);
    resultAShare =
        49.11 +
        endorsementShift +
        marketShift25 +
        (Q.pres_2025_incumbent
            ? (Number(Q.pres_2025_incumbent_record) || 0) * 0.55
            : 0) +
        ((Number(Q.ko_relation) || 50) - 50) * 0.018 +
        ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.012 -
        (Q.razem_split ? 0.28 : 0) +
        breachShift25 +
        Q.pres_2025_runoff_variance;
} else {
    const profiles = {
        ko: [55, 68, 85],
        right: [65, 25, 35],
        left: [25, 85, 80],
        razem: [15, 88, 75],
        mentzen: [88, 28, 24],
        braun: [75, 5, 5],
        holownia: [55, 60, 80],
        stanowski: [70, 42, 45],
        other: [50, 50, 50]
    };
    const affinity = function(source, target) {
        const voter = profiles[source] || profiles.other;
        const candidate = profiles[target] || profiles.other;
        return Math.max(
            5,
            100 -
                Math.abs(voter[0] - candidate[0]) * 0.35 -
                Math.abs(voter[1] - candidate[1]) * 0.35 -
                Math.abs(voter[2] - candidate[2]) * 0.30
        );
    };
    let votesA = Q.pres_2025_runoff_r1_a * 0.98;
    let votesB = Q.pres_2025_runoff_r1_b * 0.98;
    const sourceKeys = allSourceKeys25;
    for (const source of sourceKeys) {
        if (source == resultAKey || source == resultBKey) continue;
        const sourceShare =
            Math.max(0, Number(Q["pres_2025_r1_" + source]) || 0);
        const affinityA = affinity(source, resultAKey);
        const affinityB = affinity(source, resultBKey);
        const transferTurnout = Math.max(
            0.55,
            Math.min(0.94, 0.54 + Math.max(affinityA, affinityB) / 240)
        );
        const transferable = sourceShare * transferTurnout;
        let toA = transferable * affinityA / (affinityA + affinityB);
        let toB = transferable - toA;
        const boost25 = tradeBoost25(source);
        const boostToTarget25 =
            supportTarget == resultAKey || supportTarget == resultBKey;
        if (boost25 > 0 && boostToTarget25) {
            // Extra support first wakes people who were staying home, then
            // takes the harder votes off the other finalist.
            let extra25 = sourceShare * boost25;
            const idle25 = Math.max(0, sourceShare - toA - toB);
            if (supportTarget == resultAKey) {
                const wakened = Math.min(idle25, extra25 * 0.7);
                toA += wakened;
                extra25 -= wakened;
                const switched = Math.min(toB, extra25);
                toB -= switched;
                toA += switched;
            } else {
                const wakened = Math.min(idle25, extra25 * 0.7);
                toB += wakened;
                extra25 -= wakened;
                const switched = Math.min(toA, extra25);
                toA -= switched;
                toB += switched;
            }
        }
        votesA += toA;
        votesB += toB;
    }
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_transfer_a = Math.round(
        (votesA - Q.pres_2025_runoff_r1_a * 0.98) * 100
    ) / 100;
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_transfer_b = Math.round(
        (votesB - Q.pres_2025_runoff_r1_b * 0.98) * 100
    ) / 100;
    const validTransferTotal = Math.max(1, votesA + votesB);
    const endorsementShift = supportTarget == resultAKey
        ? (Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0)
        : (supportTarget == resultBKey
            ? -(Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0)
            : 0);
    const turnoutShift = supportTarget == resultAKey
        ? ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.01
        : (supportTarget == resultBKey
            ? -((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.01
            : 0);
    const marketShift25 = supportTarget == resultAKey
        ? targetBonus25
        : (supportTarget == resultBKey ? -targetBonus25 : 0);
    resultAShare =
        votesA * 100 / validTransferTotal +
        endorsementShift + turnoutShift + marketShift25 + breachShift25 +
        Q.pres_2025_runoff_variance;
}
resultAShare = historicalKoRight
    ? Math.max(42, Math.min(58, resultAShare))
    : Math.max(0, Math.min(100, resultAShare));
const resultBShare = 100 - resultAShare;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_key = resultAKey;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_key = resultBKey;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_name = finalistNames[resultAKey];
Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_name = finalistNames[resultBKey];
if (runoffMode25 == "poll") {
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_a = Math.round(resultAShare * 10) / 10;
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_b = Math.round(
        (100 - Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_a) * 10
    ) / 10;
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_margin = Math.round(
        Math.abs(
            Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_a - Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_b
        ) * 10
    ) / 10;
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_leader =
        Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_a >= Q.pres_2025_runoff_poll_b
            ? Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_name
            : Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_name;
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_support_name = supportTarget == "none"
        ? "No candidate"
        : (finalistNames[supportTarget] || "No candidate");
}
if (runoffMode25 == "result") {
Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_share =
    Math.round(resultAShare * 100) / 100;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_share =
    Math.round(resultBShare * 100) / 100;
const clampRunoffTurnout25 = function(value, low, high) {
    return Math.max(low, Math.min(high, Number(value) || 0));
};
const formatRunoffVotes25 = function(value) {
    return String(Math.round(value)).replace(
        /\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g,
        " "
    );
};
const turnoutRunoff25 = clampRunoffTurnout25(
    69.2 +
        ((Number(Q.turnout_readiness) || 58) - 58) * 0.042 +
        (Number(Q.pres_2025_transfer_strength) || 0) * 0.28 +
        (Number(Q.pres_2025_runoff_turnout_shock) || 0),
    60,
    78
);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_turnout = Math.round(turnoutRunoff25 * 100) / 100;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes = Math.round(
    20950000 * turnoutRunoff25 / 69.2
);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_a = Math.floor(
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes * resultAShare / 100
);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_b =
    Q.pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes - Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_a;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_a_display =
    formatRunoffVotes25(Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_a);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_b_display =
    formatRunoffVotes25(Q.pres_2025_runoff_votes_b);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes_display =
    formatRunoffVotes25(Q.pres_2025_runoff_valid_votes);
Q.pres_2025_runoff_margin = Math.round(
    Math.abs(resultAShare - resultBShare) * 100
) / 100;
if (resultAShare > 50) {
    Q.pres_2025_winner = Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_name;
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key = resultAKey;
} else {
    Q.pres_2025_winner = Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_name;
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key = resultBKey;
}
const presWinnerImages2025 = {
    "Rafał Trzaskowski": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-trzaskowski-2025.webp",
    "Radosław Sikorski": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-sikorski.webp",
    "Barbara Nowacka": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-nowacka.webp",
    "Karol Nawrocki": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-nawrocki.webp",
    "Mateusz Morawiecki": "img/poland/cards/advisor-morawiecki.webp",
    "Przemysław Czarnek": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-czarnek.webp",
    "Tobiasz Bocheński": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bochenski.webp",
    "Magdalena Biejat": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-biejat-2025.webp",
    "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk": "img/poland/cards/advisor-dziemianowicz-bak.webp",
    "Adrian Zandberg": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-zandberg-2025.webp",
    "Sławomir Mentzen": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-mentzen-2025.webp",
    "Krzysztof Bosak": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-bosak.webp",
    "Grzegorz Braun": "img/poland/events/grzegorz-braun-2025.webp",
    "Szymon Hołownia": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-holownia-2025.webp",
    "Ryszard Petru": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-petru.webp",
    "Krzysztof Stanowski": "img/poland/events/pres-candidate-stanowski.webp"
};
this.game.scenes[
    "poland_events_2025_pres25_runoff_campaign.presidential_runoff_2025"
].faceImage = ["right", "mentzen", "braun"].includes(
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key
)
    ? "img/poland/events/wajda.jpg"
    : presWinnerImages2025[Q.pres_2025_winner] ||
        "img/poland/events/presidential-ballot-2025.webp";
Q.pres_2025_hostile_president =
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key == "right" ||
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key == "mentzen" ||
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key == "braun" ? 1 : 0;
Q.pres_2025_runoff_done = 1;
// A presidential verdict moves the whole climate. A hostile Palace licenses
// the conservative side of every rights argument; a left or democratic win
// gives the same arguments a national mandate.
const presMoodSwing2025 = Q.pres_2025_hostile_president
    ? -1
    : (Q.pres_2025_winner_key == "left" || Q.pres_2025_winner_key == "razem"
        ? 1.35
        : 0.6);
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_support += Math.round(12 * presMoodSwing2025);
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_support += Math.round(13 * presMoodSwing2025);
Q.public_mood_pending_secular_state_support += Math.round(10 * presMoodSwing2025);
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += Math.round(9 * presMoodSwing2025);
Q.public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += Math.round(8 * presMoodSwing2025);
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 12;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 12;
Q.public_mood_pending_secular_state_salience += 9;
Q.public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 9;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += Q.pres_2025_hostile_president ? 10 : 6;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_backlash += Q.pres_2025_hostile_president ? 9 : 5;
Q.news_headline = Q.pres_2025_winner + " wins the presidential runoff";
// Only the two finalists have anything left to resolve; every other row keeps
// the status the first-round table already gave it.
Q["pres_2025_status_" + resultAKey] =
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key == resultAKey ? "elected" : "defeated";
Q["pres_2025_status_" + resultBKey] =
    Q.pres_2025_winner_key == resultBKey ? "elected" : "defeated";
const presidentialRunoffMapModel25 = (typeof window !== "undefined"
    ? window : globalThis).polandElectionModel;
const presidentialFamily25 = function(id) {
    if (id == "ko") return "ko";
    if (id == "right") return "pis";
    if (id == "left" || id == "razem") return "left";
    if (id == "mentzen" || id == "braun") return "konf";
    if (id == "holownia") return "p2050";
    return "other";
};
presidentialRunoffMapModel25.archivePresident(Q,
    presidentialRunoffMapModel25.allocatePresident({
        state: Q,
        key: "2025-06-r2",
        label: "2025 presidential election — runoff",
        round: 2,
        candidates: [
            {id: resultAKey, name: Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_name,
                family: presidentialFamily25(resultAKey),
                share: Q.pres_2025_runoff_a_share},
            {id: resultBKey, name: Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_name,
                family: presidentialFamily25(resultBKey),
                share: Q.pres_2025_runoff_b_share}
        ]
    })
);
}
!}
